course: dictionary
lesson: 10042
title: Terrain: the shape of the land
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Terrain is a word for the land you walk on or look at. Is it hilly, rocky, flat, muddy or rough? Think of terrain as the shape and surface of the ground.
explain: Read the words around it. «EU5 shows hills and mountains as terrain pictures» tells you terrain is about land, because hills and mountains are things you find on land. You can check by swapping in a simple word: hills and mountains as land pictures still makes sense.
explain: Terrain can also mean an area of knowledge or activity. «Algebra was new terrain for her» means maths was a new subject she had not explored before. The word new is the clue.
fact: Terrain means a stretch of land and what it is like.
fact: Terrain can be hilly, rocky, flat, muddy or rough.
fact: Rough terrain makes journeys hard, so walkers and explorers plan carefully.
fact: An all-terrain vehicle can travel over any kind of ground.
fact: In geography, terrain is described by its features, such as mountains, valleys, plains and deserts.
exercise: «EU5 shows hills and mountains as terrain pictures.» What does terrain mean here? | A type of video game score | A kind of picture drawn by a child | A key on a map | *The land itself, with its hills and mountains
exercise: A hiker says the path has rocky terrain. What does rocky terrain mean? | *Land covered with rocks, which is hard to walk over | Soft grass for a picnic | Calm, deep water | A busy road in the city
exercise: «Algebra was new terrain for her.» What does terrain mean in this sentence? | A fast running race | *An area of knowledge she had not explored before | A sandy beach | A hill covered in trees
test: Which of these is the best example of difficult terrain? | A flat football pitch | *Deep mud, steep rocks and loose stones | A carpet in a bedroom | Smooth tarmac in a car park
test: What is an all-terrain vehicle? | *A vehicle that can travel over any kind of ground | A car that can only drive on roads | A toy car for a bedroom | A bus for a city
exam: What does terrain describe? | The colour of the sky | The speed of a car | The weather today | *The shape and surface of the land
